Per-file headers in improve/src/ name the Backpass module each file was
adapted from. Actual adapted source mappings in this slice:

  - improve/src/analyze.js <- Backpass src/acpx.js + src/analyze.js
  - improve/src/discovery.js <- Backpass src/discovery/index.js + src/discovery/adapters/{hermes,pi,claude,codex,opencode}.js
  - improve/src/distill.js <- Backpass src/distill.js
  - improve/src/fold.js <- Backpass src/fold.js
  - improve/src/sentinel.js <- Backpass src/sentinel.js
  - improve/src/synthesize.js <- Backpass src/synthesize.js + src/proposal.js

CA-native (not adapted from Backpass, excluded from the above):

  - improve/src/pipeline.js (CA headless propose-only orchestration)
  - improve/src/state.js (CA XDG private state: cursor/run state, evidence, ledger, proposal)
  - improve/bin/ca-improve.js (CA narrow JSON CLI boundary)

The CA runtime intentionally diverges: it trains only
durable experience records (never SOUL/memory files directly), supports a
narrow harness set (hermes, pi, claude, codex, opencode), and keeps all
private state under XDG_DATA_HOME.
